{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Premise validated in fresh worktree harrier-typing (base ae6f2ac57a). Siblings had already annotated most of the package: baseline `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` reported only 13 errors, ALL in authorship.py; the other 6 attest files were already clean. Scope adapted accordingly — the change touches authorship.py only.\n\nAnnotations applied (annotations-only, zero runtime effect — the module carries `from __future__ import annotations`, so these are never evaluated):\n- 12 def sites: bare `repo_root=None` -> `repo_root: str | None = None`, matching the convention already established elsewhere in the package (trusted_env.py:49/62/68/124, opcert.py:185).\n- keys_valid_at_anchor: `resolve` -> `Callable[[str], str | None]`, `is_ancestor` -> `Callable[[str, str], bool]` — types read off the docstring contract and confirmed against both call sites (authorship.verify_authorship_at_commit's local _resolve/_is_ancestor, and opcert.verify_opcert:296).\n- verify_authorship_at_commit: `position_resolver` -> `Callable[[str], str | None] | None`, confirmed against _commands/verify_authorship.py:565 _resolve_position.\n- _keyring_for return tightened `list` -> `list[dict]` (it already had an annotation; tightened while in the neighborhood since the body provably returns list-of-dict records).\n- Added `from collections.abc import Callable`.\n\nAC status: (1) `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` -> Success, no issues in 7 source files. Independently cross-checked with an AST walk asserting no unannotated params remain. (2) Any-count grep reports exactly 2 (unchanged — the registry.py trust_root boundary); no new Any introduced. (3) pyproject.toml untouched (`git diff --stat -- pyproject.toml` empty).\n\nGates so far: make lint PASS (after `ruff format` rewrapped 4 signatures that crossed the line-length limit), make typecheck PASS (518 files), check_* gates PASS. Full CI pytest lane still running."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786597404416032001,"uuid":"8ace7ac5-42aa-4699-aec9-edf74e737838"}